{"agent":"lane-sec-gate-env","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"With `gates.scrub_secret_names = \"on\"` — the knob’s declared `strictest` value — and the default `secret_name_patterns`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` matches `_API_KEY` and is removed from the gate/CI child environment. Project rule [r-gemini-key-load] requires the Gemini reviewer key to be exported into the child before a review, because otherwise the gemini reviewer sends no key and requests fail. Thus the “strictest” recommendation encourages a configuration that breaks required gemini reviews unless the operator also manually adds `GEMINI_API_KEY` to `keep_env`; the knob should exempt required `api_key_env` variables or make that requirement explicit.","digest":"0cb480d65c3213dd","family":"alibaba","location":"`ddflow/config_sections/gates.py` `scrub_secret_names`","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"`ddflow/config_sections/gates.py` `scrub_secret_names`"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The doctor note claims that setting `gates.scrub_secret_names = \"on\"` removes the listed names from “every gate and CI child” and mentions only `[gates].keep_env` as an exception. But `[ci].keep_env` also preserves variables in CI children. For example, with `secret_name_patterns = [\"TOKEN\"]`, `ci.keep_env = [\"GITHUB_TOKEN\"]`, and a non-CI gate run that recorded `env_secret_mode = \"warn\"` and `env_secret_names = [\"GITHUB_TOKEN\"]`, `doctor_notes` emits the note. If the operator follows it and sets scrubbing on, `child_env(..., ci=True)` will still preserve `GITHUB_TOKEN` because `[ci].keep_env` is consulted, so the note’s “CI child” claim is false.","digest":"60d4c0b656f6550d","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/gateenv.py:doctor_notes","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/gateenv.py:doctor_notes"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The documented per-run override `DDFLOW_GATES_SCRUB_SECRET_NAMES=on` contains the default secret-name fragment `_SECRET` (case-blind substring match). Therefore, with the documented default patterns, the scrubber treats its own configuration override as a secret-shaped variable: in `warn` mode the gate evidence/doctor reports `DDFLOW_GATES_SCRUB_SECRET_NAMES` as a secret-shaped name even though it is only a knob setting, and in `on` mode the variable is removed from child environments, so a nested `ddflow`/gate child does not see the per-run setting that enabled scrubbing. The change should exclude ddflow’s own config environment variables (or avoid matching the override variable name) instead of scrubbing/warning the control variable itself.","digest":"9b64b79eafd39d62","family":"alibaba","location":"docs/guide/configuration.md (added `DDFLOW_GATES_SCRUB_SECRET_NAMES` / default `secret_name_patterns`)","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"docs/guide/configuration.md (added `DDFLOW_GATES_SCRUB_SECRET_NAMES` / default `secret_name_patterns`)"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":18628,"diff_sha":"f546da253963ece641ab2431d4fc2d6a7ed33760d7d3e9a92c8946730599329d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/SEC-gate-env-secrets","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":376.1,"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"c57492536acf5896","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SEC-gate-env-secrets.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T202029Z-1e42478c.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"1ac4b266289799a72597fa0003b860b62432d9d9","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/reporting/health.py":"100644 c00ac7512d436916a95b12ee43b46c62302bf68c","ddflow/config_sections/gates.py":"100644 19a0578502ceef385200efee1b9abd00b5c31138","ddflow/services/gateenv.py":"100644 d01f2e9c0290deb078e467